{"id":"nl0.json","pointer":"/propositions","view":"value","value":[{"id":"H001","kind":"hypothesis","definitions":[],"objects":["p","K"],"binders":[],"statement":"p is a prime number and K has characteristic p."},{"id":"H002","kind":"hypothesis","definitions":[],"objects":["λ","p"],"binders":[],"statement":"λ is an integer satisfying 0≤λ<p."},{"id":"H003","kind":"hypothesis","definitions":[],"objects":["V","λ","x","y","h"],"binders":[],"statement":"V is the complex irreducible highest-weight sl₂(ℂ)-module of highest weight λ, of complex dimension λ+1. The Chevalley generators x,y,h of sl₂(ℂ) act on V and satisfy [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=−2y, [x,y]=h. In its universal enveloping algebra and in the induced operators on V, the bracket is [a,b]=ab−ba; the same symbols denote the corresponding operators."},{"id":"H004","kind":"hypothesis","definitions":[],"objects":["V","v","x","h","λ"],"binders":[],"statement":"v∈V is nonzero, xv=0, and hv=λv."},{"id":"H005","kind":"hypothesis","definitions":["D005"],"objects":["M","V","U_Z"],"binders":[],"statement":"M⊂V is an arbitrary admissible lattice: a free abelian subgroup admitting an integer basis which is also a complex basis of V, and stable under U_Z. No minimal-lattice assumption is imposed."},{"id":"M001","kind":"mathlib","statement":"Let A be a semiring satisfying the strong rank condition (every injective linear map between finite free A-modules has source rank at most target rank), let B be a finite index type, and for each t∈B let C_t be an additive commutative monoid with an A-module structure, free and finitely generated over A. Then finrank_A(∏_{t∈B} C_t)=∑_{t∈B} finrank_A(C_t). Here finrank is cardinal module rank converted to a natural number (zero if that cardinal is infinite).","definitions":[],"binders":[{"symbol":"A","type":"semiring"},{"symbol":"B","type":"finite index type"},{"symbol":"C","type":"family of additive commutative monoids indexed by B"},{"symbol":"t","type":"element of B"}],"objects":["A","B","C","t"],"source":{"declaration":"Module.finrank_pi_fintype","hypotheses":["A is a semiring satisfying the strong rank condition.","B is finite.","Each C_t is an additive commutative monoid with an A-module structure.","Each C_t is free and finitely generated as an A-module."],"statement":"Let A be a semiring satisfying the strong rank condition (every injective linear map between finite free A-modules has source rank at most target rank), let B be a finite index type, and for each t∈B let C_t be an additive commutative monoid with an A-module structure, free and finitely generated over A. Then finrank_A(∏_{t∈B} C_t)=∑_{t∈B} finrank_A(C_t). Here finrank is cardinal module rank converted to a natural number (zero if that cardinal is infinite).","module":"Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","signature":"@Module.finrank_pi_fintype : ∀ (R : Type u) [inst : Semiring.{u} R] [StrongRankCondition.{u} R] {ι : Type v} [inst_2 : Fintype.{v} ι]\n  {M : ι → Type w} [inst_3 : (i : ι) → AddCommMonoid.{w} (M i)] [inst_4 : (i : ι) → _root_.Module.{u, w} R (M i)]\n  [∀ (i : ι), Module.Free.{u, w} R (M i)] [∀ (i : ι), Module.Finite.{u, w} R (M i)],\n  Eq.{1} (Module.finrank.{u, max v w} R ((i : ι) → M i)) (∑ i, Module.finrank.{u, w} R (M i))","declaration_kind":"theorem","mathlib_commit":"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c","source_path":"Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Dimension/Constructions.lean","source_sha256":"395f49a423c4c46bb246eb11c785cbc350b3f938b1fa8b7e840635b208953e10","evidence":[{"path":"library/M001-0001/library-sources.json","sha256":"eee515576db994f4326b0cccef71b92b3d2bf3baa3f2cc5ccfa161ad7729972a"}]}},{"id":"M002","kind":"mathlib","statement":"Let A be a semiring, B a commutative semiring, both satisfying the strong rank condition (an injective linear map between finite free modules has source rank at most target rank), and C an additive commutative monoid with a free B-module structure. Given a B-algebra structure on A, finrank_A(A⊗_B C)=finrank_B(C). Here finrank is cardinal module rank converted to a natural number (zero if infinite); C need not be finitely generated.","definitions":[],"binders":[{"symbol":"A","type":"semiring"},{"symbol":"B","type":"commutative semiring"},{"symbol":"C","type":"additive commutative monoid"}],"objects":["A","B","C"],"source":{"declaration":"Module.finrank_baseChange","hypotheses":["A is a semiring and B is a commutative semiring, both satisfying the strong rank condition.","C is an additive commutative monoid with a free B-module structure.","A carries a B-algebra structure."],"statement":"Let A be a semiring, B a commutative semiring, both satisfying the strong rank condition (an injective linear map between finite free modules has source rank at most target rank), and C an additive commutative monoid with a free B-module structure. Given a B-algebra structure on A, finrank_A(A⊗_B C)=finrank_B(C). Here finrank is cardinal module rank converted to a natural number (zero if infinite); C need not be finitely generated.","module":"Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","signature":"@Module.finrank_baseChange : ∀ {R : Type u} {S : Type u'} {M' : Type v'} [inst : Semiring.{u} R] [inst_1 : CommSemiring.{u'} S]\n  [inst_2 : AddCommMonoid.{v'} M'] [StrongRankCondition.{u} R] [StrongRankCondition.{u'} S]\n  [inst_5 : _root_.Module.{u', v'} S M'] [Module.Free.{u', v'} S M'] [inst_7 : Algebra.{u', u} S R],\n  Eq.{1} (Module.finrank.{u, max v' u} R (TensorProduct.{u', u, v'} S R M')) (Module.finrank.{u', v'} S M')","declaration_kind":"theorem","mathlib_commit":"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c","source_path":"Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Dimension/Constructions.lean","source_sha256":"395f49a423c4c46bb246eb11c785cbc350b3f938b1fa8b7e840635b208953e10","evidence":[{"path":"library/M002-0002/library-sources.json","sha256":"48c51156444fbfd7be7fdb5dc9a492adb9224aa2b702d4c01ecca942cf015806"}]}},{"id":"N001","kind":"internal","statement":"n=λ+1>0 and |I|=n. For every integer t≥0, h y^t v=(λ−2t)y^t v; for t≥1, x y^t v=t(λ−t+1)y^(t−1)v. The vectors (e_i)_{i∈I} form a complex basis of V, and y^(λ+1)v=0 (hence all higher lowering powers vanish). On this basis, xe_0=0, xe_i=(λ−i+1)e_(i−1) for 1≤i≤λ, ye_i=(i+1)e_(i+1) for 0≤i<λ, ye_λ=0, he_i=(λ−2i)e_i. For all i∈I and natural r, X_r e_i=binom(λ−i+r,r)e_(i−r) if r≤i and zero otherwise; Y_r e_i=binom(i+r,r)e_(i+r) if i+r≤λ and zero otherwise. All displayed divided-power coefficients are integers.","definitions":["D001","D002","D003","D004","D006"],"objects":["n","λ","I","V","v","x","y","h","e","X","Y"],"binders":[{"symbol":"t","type":"nonnegative integer"},{"symbol":"i","type":"element of I"},{"symbol":"r","type":"natural number"}],"origin":"problem.md:45-84"},{"id":"N002","kind":"internal","statement":"iota embeds M_R as the R-span of M in V; M_R is free of rank n over R and its complex span is V. Each X_r and Y_r (r≥0) preserves M and M_R, and x,y,h preserve M and M_R. For every i,j∈I, E_ij preserves M_R (under iota). The following identities hold on V: Pi=Y_λ X_λ=E_λλ, X_(λ−i)Pi=E_iλ, Pi Y_(λ−j)=binom(λ,j)E_λj, and E_ij=binom(λ,j)^(-1) X_(λ−i)Pi Y_(λ−j), where binom(λ,j) is a unit in R.","definitions":["D001","D002","D003","D004","D006","D007","D008","D009","D010","D011"],"objects":["n","R","M","M_R","iota","V","X","Y","x","y","h","I","E","Pi","λ"],"binders":[{"symbol":"r","type":"natural number"},{"symbol":"i","type":"element of I"},{"symbol":"j","type":"element of I"}],"origin":"problem.md:86-116; lattice-operator well-definedness from admissibility"},{"id":"N003","kind":"internal","statement":"For every i∈I one has J_i=J. The R-module J⊂ℂ is nonzero and finitely generated. The map (c_i)_{i∈I}↦∑_{i∈I}c_i e_i is an R-linear isomorphism ∏_{i∈I}J→iota(M_R), so, identifying M_R through iota, M_R=⊕_{i∈I}J e_i.","definitions":["D002","D006","D007","D008","D009","D012","D013"],"objects":["I","J_i","J","R","e","iota","M_R"],"binders":[{"symbol":"i","type":"element of I"},{"symbol":"c","type":"I-indexed family of elements of J"}],"origin":"problem.md:118-130"},{"id":"N004","kind":"internal","statement":"The multiplication map ℚ⊗_R J→ℂ is injective and its image is the rational span of J, a one-dimensional ℚ-vector space. There exists b∈J with b≠0 and J=Rb. For any such b, the family (b e_i)_{i∈I} is an R-basis of M_R identified with iota(M_R).","definitions":["D002","D006","D007","D008","D009","D013"],"objects":["R","J","I","e","M_R","iota"],"binders":[{"symbol":"b","type":"complex number"},{"symbol":"i","type":"element of I"}],"origin":"problem.md:132-148"},{"id":"N005","kind":"internal","statement":"The natural tensor maps give K-linear isomorphisms V_K≅M_R⊗_R K≅(M_R/pM_R)⊗_(F_p)K, intertwining all lattice operators. There exists a K-basis (b_i)_{i∈I} of V_K obtained from an R-basis (b e_i) of M_R with b∈J nonzero. In particular dim_K(V_K)=n=λ+1>0. On this basis the induced operators satisfy xb_0=0, xb_i=(λ−i+1)b_(i−1) for 1≤i≤λ, yb_i=(i+1)b_(i+1) for i<λ, yb_λ=0, hb_i=(λ−2i)b_i, with integer coefficients interpreted in K. For every 0≤r≤λ, r! is nonzero in K and the induced divided powers X_r,Y_r equal (r!)^(-1)x^r,(r!)^(-1)y^r. Every binom(λ,j) for j∈I is nonzero in K. The reduced operators T_ij=binom(λ,j)^(-1) X_(λ−i)(Y_λ X_λ)Y_(λ−j), for i,j∈I, obey T_ij b_k=δ_jk b_i for every k∈I, where δ_jk is 1 for j=k and 0 otherwise.","definitions":["D001","D002","D003","D004","D006","D007","D008","D009","D013","D014","D016","D017"],"objects":["K","V_K","M_R","p","F_p","I","e","J","n","λ","x","y","h","X","Y","R","kappa","iota"],"binders":[{"symbol":"b","type":"complex number"},{"symbol":"b_i","type":"I-indexed family of vectors of V_K"},{"symbol":"i","type":"element of I"},{"symbol":"j","type":"element of I"},{"symbol":"k","type":"element of I"},{"symbol":"r","type":"integer"},{"symbol":"T","type":"I×I-indexed family of K-linear endomorphisms of V_K"}],"origin":"problem.md:150-170"},{"id":"P","kind":"target","definitions":["D014","D015"],"binders":[{"symbol":"W","type":"K-linear subspace of V_K"}],"objects":["V_K","L_K","K","W","x","y","h","p","λ","M"],"statement":"V_K is nonzero, and for every K-linear subspace W⊆V_K, if W is invariant under the induced x,y,h then W={0} or W=V_K. Equivalently V(K) is irreducible as an L(K)-module. This holds for every given prime p, field K of characteristic p, integer 0≤λ<p, and arbitrary admissible lattice M, including λ=0 and p=2, without assuming K algebraically closed."}],"has_more":false,"next_offset":null}
